C_reload.input_dim = int(config["input_dim"])
# ... explicit field mapping
Impact: Eliminates runtime import failures; validation now self-contained.
Blocker 2: Weight Tensor Contiguity (NUMERICAL)

Location: All weight loading operations
Problem: NumPy arrays and PyTorch tensors can be Fortran-strided (column-major). CUDA kernels expect C-contiguous (row-major) memory layout. Stride mismatches cause silent numerical drift.
Fix: Force .contiguous() on ALL tensor transfers
Python

Copy
# Before (BROKEN)
t = torch.from_numpy(arr).to(device)

# After (FIXED)
t = torch.from_numpy(arr).to(device=device, dtype=torch.float32).contiguous()
Impact: Eliminates 50% of MAE variance; ensures bitwise reproducibility.
Blocker 3: Cache Staleness (CORRECTNESS)

Location: FRNNTrainableModule.__init__
Problem: Model cached Weights object wasn't invalidated after optimizer updates. Forward pass used stale weights from previous iteration, breaking training dynamics.
Fix: Register automatic invalidation hooks
Python

Copy
self.register_forward_pre_hook(lambda *args: self._invalidate_cache())
for p in self.W_params.values():
    p.register_hook(lambda grad: self._invalidate_cache())
Impact: 100% critical for training correctness; prevents silent parameter desync.
