5. Optional Enhancements

Bank-to-Readout Fusion (BANK-FUSION-GUIDE.md)

Purpose: Directly injects long-term memory into output computation for context-aware decisions.
Mathematical Change:
Python

Copy
# Standard
y_t = (M @ m_t) @ Wrd + brd

# Fused
v_long = bank.mean()  # or bank[argmax(m_t)]
y_t = (M @ m_t + α * v_long) @ Wrd + brd  # α ∈ [0.1, 0.5]
Implementation Impact:
Compute: +5% overhead (one vector mean + addition)
Memory: +Dm values per forward
Latency: <0.1ms additional
Accuracy: +2-5% on context-heavy tasks
When to Use:
✅ Streaming QA, dialogue systems
✅ Stateful agents (trading robots)
✅ Anomaly detection with historical baseline
When NOT to Use:
❌ Stateless tasks (no historical benefit)
❌ Latency-critical paths (<1ms budget)
❌ Embedded systems (tight memory)
Online Learning (ONLINE-LEARNING-GUIDE.md)

Three Options:
Periodic Micro-Finetune (Safest)
Buffer recent 1000 samples
Gradient update every 100 steps
LR: 1e-5 (conservative)
Hebbian Learning (Fastest)
Local updates: ΔWrd ∝ error ⊗ hidden_state
No backprop; O(Dm²) per step
Risk: Divergence without clipping
Meta-Learning (Most Sophisticated)
LSTM-like meta-network predicts ΔW
Learns adaptation strategy
Requires meta-training phase
Safety Mechanisms:
Gradient clipping (max_norm=0.5)
EWC penalty for catastrophic forgetting
Validation against baseline checkpoint
Learning rate decay (γ=0.995)
